vices or rely on live data. The CLI must be runnable locally and produce the three outputs at the exact paths above when given input/auctions_2026-04-18.csv.\n26\t\n27\tThis will help me quickly identify the best snipe targets and walk my team through action items during our daily bidding huddle. All file paths are relative to the workspace directory.\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14982240 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "Read", "arguments": {"file_path": "input/auctions_2026-04-18.csv"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n1\tauction_id,title,current_bid,shipping_cost,time_left_min,seller_rating,bid_increment,my_max_bid,category,watchlist_flag\n2\tA1,"Vintage Camera",120,15,45,99.2,2.5,180,collectibles,1\n3\tA2,"Gaming GPU",300,20,25,98.5,5,360,electronics,1\n4\tA3,"Rare Coin",75,5,170,97.5,1,150,collectibles,1\n5\tA4,"Smartphone",200,10,190,99.0,2,250,electronics,1\n6\tA5,"Drone",220,5,60,96.0,5,300,electronics,1\n7\tA6,"Vintage Vinyl",40,10,15,98.0,1,70,collectibles,1\n8\tA7,"Pro Keyboard",90,10,85,99.5,2,110,electronics,1\n9\tA8,"Collectible Comic",160,0,50,99.8,1,159,collectibles,1\n10\tA9,"VR Headset",180,15,35,97.2,2,220,electronics,0\n11\tA10,"Action Figure Set",45,5,30,98.7,1,80,collectibles,1\n12\t\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14981357 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nI\'ll implement the auction processing CLI as specified in the PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md. Let me start by analyzing the requirements and creating the solution.\n\nThe task requires:\n1. Filtering auctions based on specific criteria\n2. Scoring and ranking candidates using a formula\n3. Creating three outputs: a ranked CSV, meeting notes, and a process log\n\nI\'ll create the solution by writing the necessary Python code to process the CSV file according to the specifications.\n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "Write", "arguments": {"file_path": "bin/process_auctions.py", "content": "import csv\\nimport json\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\n\\ndef process_auctions(input_file, output_dir):\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    Process auction data according to specified criteria and requirements.\\n    \\"\\"\\"\\n    # Read the input CSV\\n    with open(input_file, \'r\', encoding=\'utf-8\') as f:\\n        reader = csv.DictReader(f)\\n        rows = list(reader)\\n    \\n    # Filter rows based on requirements\\n    filtered_rows = []\\n    for row in rows:\\n        # Check all filter criteria\\n        if (int(row[\'watchlist_flag\']) == 1 and\\n            int(row[\'time_left_min\']) <= 180 and\\n            float(row[\'seller_rating\']) >= 97.0 and\\n            (float(row[\'current_bid\']) + float(row[\'shipping_cost\'])) < float(row[\'my_max_bid\'])):\\n            filtered_rows.append(row)\\n    \\n    # Calculate scores and rank\\n    ranked_rows = []\\n    for row in filtered_rows:\\n        current_bid = float(row[\'current_bid\'])\\n        shipping_cost = float(row[\'shipping_cost\'])\\n        time_left_min = int(row[\'time_left_min\'])\\n        seller_rating = float(row[\'seller_rating\'])\\n        bid_increment = float(row[\'bid_increment\'])\\n        my_max_bid = float(row[\'my_max_bid\'])\\n        \\n        # Calculate affordability margin\\n        affordability_margin = my_max_bid - (current_bid + shipping_cost)\\n        \\n        # Calculate urgency points\\n        if time_left_min <= 30:\\n            urgency_points = 3\\n        elif time_left_min <= 60:\\n            urgency_points = 2\\n        elif time_left_min <= 180:\\n            urgency_points = 1\\n        else:\\n            urgency_points = 0\\n        \\n        # Calculate score\\n        score = (0.5 * affordability_margin) + (10 * (seller_rating / 100)) + (5 * urgency_points) - (0.5 * bid_increment)\\n        \\n        # Create a new dictionary with all the calculated fields\\n        new_row = {\\n            \'auction_id\': row[\'auction_id\'],\\n            \'title\': row[\'title\'],\\n            \'current_bid\': current_bid,\\n            \'shipping_cost\': shipping_cost,\\n            \'time_left_min\': time_left_min,\\n            \'seller_rating\': seller_rating,\\n            \'bid_increment\': bid_increment,\\n            \'my_max_bid\': my_max_bid,\\n            \'affordability_margin\': affordability_margin,\\n            \'urgency_points\': urgency_points,\\n            \'score\': score,\\n            \'rank\': None  # Will be set during ranking\\n        }\\n        ranked_rows.append(new_row)\\n    \\n    # Sort by score descending, then by time_left_min ascending, then by current_bid ascending\\n    ranked_rows.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[\'score\'], x[\'time_left_min\'], x[\'current_bid\']))\\n    \\n    # Assign ranks\\n    for i, row in enumerate(ranked_rows):\\n        row[\'rank\'] = i + 1\\n    \\n    # Extract top 5\\n    top5 = ranked_rows[:5]\\n    \\n    # Create output directory if it doesn\'t exist\\n    import os\\n    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n    \\n    # Create candidates.csv\\n    candidates_csv_path = os.path.join(output_dir, \'candidates.csv\')\\n    with open(candidates_csv_path, \'w\', encoding=\'utf-8\') as f:\\n        writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=[\\n            \'auction_id\', \'title\', \'current_bid\', \'shipping_cost\',\\n            \'time_left_min\', \'seller_rating\', \'bid_increment\',\\n            \'my_max_bid\', \'affordability_margin\', \'urgency_points\',\\n            \'score\', \'rank\'\\n        ], quoting=csv.QUOTE_ALL)\\n        writer.writeheader()\\n        writer.writerows(top5)\\n    \\n    # Create meeting_notes.md\\n    meeting_notes_path = os.path.join(output_dir, \'meeting_notes.md\')\\n    timestamp = datetime.now().isoformat()\\n    \\n    with open(meeting_notes_path, \'w\', encoding=\'utf-8\') as f:\\n        f.write(f\\"## Summary\\n- Run timestamp: {timestamp}\\n- Input file: {input_file}\\n- Total rows parsed: {len(rows)}\\n- Rows kept after filters: {len(filtered_rows)}\\n- Ranking formula: score = 0.5*affordability_margin + 10*(seller_rating/100) + 5*urgency_points - 0.5*bid_increment\\\\n\\\\n\\")\\n        f.write(\\"## Top Targets\\\\n\\")\\n        for row in top5:\\n            rank = row[\'rank\']\\n            auction_id = row[\'auction_id\']\\n            title = row[\'title\']\\n            score = round(row[\'score\'], 2)\\n            time_left_min = row[\'time_left_min\']\\n            snipe_offset_min_from_run = max(time_left_min - 1, 0)\\n            f.write(f\\"- Rank {rank}: {auction_id} - {title} - Score: {score} - Snipe offset: {snipe_offset_min_from_run} min\\\\n\\")\\n        f.write(\\"\\\\n## Action Items\\\\n\\")\\n        for row in top5:\\n            auction_id = row[\'auction_id\']\\n            title = row[\'title\']\\n            current_bid = row[\'current_bid\']\\n            shipping_cost = row[\'shipping_cost\']\\n            bid_increment = row[\'bid_increment\']\\n            my_max_bid = row[\'my_max_bid\']\\n            \\n            recommended_bid = my_max_bid - bid_increment\\n            total_cost = current_bid + shipping_cost\\n            \\n            f.write(f\\"- Prepare snipe at recommended_bid = {recommended_bid}\\\\n\\")\\n            f.write(f\\"- Verify seller feedback and item photos\\\\n\\")\\n            f.write(f\\"- Confirm total cost (current_bid + shipping_cost) is within budget\\\\n\\")\\n            f.write(f\\"  (Recommended bid: {recommended_bid}, Total cost: {total_cost})\\\\n\\")\\n            f.write(\\"\\\\n\\")\\n    \\n    # Create process_log.json\\n    process_log_path = os.path.join(output_dir, \'process_log.json\')\\n    process_log = {\\n        \'input_file\': input_file,\\n        \'processed_at\': timestamp,\\n        \'total_rows\': len(rows),\\n        \'filtered_in_rows\': len(filtered_rows),\\n        \'top5_ids\': [row[\'auction_id\'] for row in top5],\\n        \'outputs\': {\\n            \'candidates_csv\': candidates_csv_path,\\n            \'meeting_notes_md\': meeting_notes_path\\n        }\\n    }\\n    \\n    with open(process_log_path, \'w\', encoding=\'utf-8\') as f:\\n        json.dump(process_log, f, indent=2)\\n    \\n    return process_log\\n\\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n    import sys\\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3:\\n        print(\\"Usage: python process_auctions.py <input_file> <output_directory>\\")\\n        sys.exit(1)\\n    \\n    input_file = sys.argv[1]\\n    output_dir = sys.argv[2]\\n    \\n    result = process_auctions(input_file, output_dir)\\n    print(\\"Auction processing completed successfully!\\")\\n    print(f\\"Outputs written to {output_dir}\\")\\n    print(f\\"Process log: {result[\'outputs\'][\'process_log.json\']}\\")\\n    print(f\\"Candidates: {result[\'outputs\'][\'candidates.csv\']}\\")\\n    print(f\\"Meeting notes: {result[\'outputs\'][\'meeting_notes.md\']}\\")"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>'], label: clawgym_194, reward: 0.0
