(RolloutManager pid=4705) [2026-11-27 07:45:13] sglang_rollout.py:420 - First rollout sample: ['We’re applying for new business insurance and my chief asked for a concise, data-backed risk snapshot before he makes a decision. Using only the files under input/, please synthesize a facility-level risk summary and supporting artifacts. Deliverables and requirements:\n\n1) Create output/risk_metrics.csv with one row per facility and the following columns in this order:\n- facility_id\n- facility_name\n- location\n- employees\n- total_incidents\n- incident_rate_per_100_employees (round to 2 decimals)\n- total_direct_cost_usd (numeric, no currency symbols; round to 2 decimals)\n- avg_cost_per_incident_usd (round to 2 decimals; 0.00 if no incidents)\n- total_lost_time_days\n- asset_value_usd_total (round to 2 decimals)\n- audit_compliance_percent (integer 0-100 or the string MISSING if the audit file isn’t present)\n- training_completion_percent (integer 0-100 or the string UNKNOWN if not found in the HTML table)\n- composite_risk_score (round to 2 decimals) computed as:\n  composite_risk_score = incident_rate_per_100_employees\n                        + 0.2 * audit_gap\n                        + 0.1 * training_gap\n                        + cost_factor\n  where:\n  - audit_gap = 100 - audit_compliance_percent; if audit is MISSING, set audit_gap = 100.\n  - training_gap = 100 - training_completion_percent; if training is UNKNOWN, set training_gap = 100.\n  - cost_factor = min(10, total_direct_cost_usd / 10000).\n\nInputs for this CSV must be derived by:\n- Parsing input/facilities.csv for facility roster and employees.\n- Aggregating input/incidents.csv per facility: total_incidents, total_direct_cost_usd, avg_cost_per_incident_usd, total_lost_time_days.\n- Summing asset values per facility from input/assets.jsonl.\n- Inspecting the input/audits/ directory to find per-facility audit JSON files; if a facility’s audit file is missing, mark audit_compliance_percent as MISSING; otherwise parse compliance_percent from the file.\n- Extracting facility_id and training_completion_percent from the HTML table in input/training.html; if a facility isn’t present in the table, set training_completion_percent to UNKNOWN.\n\n2) Create output/audit_inventory.txt that reflects directory inspection of input/audits/ using this structure:\n- A section titled "Present audit files:" listing each found JSON file name on its own line.\n- A section titled "Facilities missing audit files:" listing each facility_id with no corresponding audit JSON file on its own line.\n\n3) Create output/risk_summary.md that a chief can skim quickly. Include:\n- A brief overview (1–3 sentences) stating inputs used and that this is for an insurance coverage decision.\n- Company-wide totals: total incidents and total direct cost across all facilities (numbers only; direct cost rounded to 2 decimals).\n- A "Top 3 facilities by composite risk score" section with a bullet list, each item including facility_id, facility_name, composite_risk_score, total_incidents, total_direct_cost_usd, audit_compliance_percent (or MISSING), and training_completion_percent (or UNKNOWN).\n- A "Gaps/Notes" section that explicitly lists facilities without audit files and any facilities lacking training records.\n\nUse only the provided input files; do not fetch anything from the Internet. All outputs should be written to the output/ directory using the exact paths above. All file paths are relative to the workspace directory.<tool_call>\n{"name": "Read", "arguments": {"file_path": "PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n1\tWe’re applying for new business insurance and my chief asked for a concise, data-backed risk snapshot before he makes a decision. Using only the files under input/, please synthesize a facility-level risk summary and supporting artifacts. Deliverables and requirements:\n2\t\n3\t1) Create output/risk_metrics.csv with one row per facility and the following columns in this order:\n4\t- facility_id\n5\t- facility_name\n6\t- location\n7\t- employees\n8\t- total_incidents\n9\t- incident_rate_per_100_employees (round to 2 decimals)\n10\t- total_direct_cost_usd (numeric, no currency symbols; round to 2 decimals)\n11\t- avg_cost_per_incident_usd (round to 2 decimals; 0.00 if no incidents)\n12\t- total_lost_time_days\n13\t- asset_value_usd_total (round to 2 decimals)\n14\t- audit_compliance_percent (integer 0-100 or the string MISSING if the audit file isn’t present)\n15\t- training_completion_percent (integer 0-100 or the string UNKNOWN if not found in the HTML table)\n16\t- composite_risk_score (round to 2 decimals) computed as:\n17\t  composite_risk_score = incident_rate_per_100_employees\n18\t                        + 0.2 * audit_gap\n19\t                        + 0.1 * training_gap\n20\t                        + cost_factor\n21\t  where:\n22\t  - audit_gap = 100 - audit_compliance_percent; if audit is MISSING, set audit_gap = 100.\n23\t  - training_gap = 100 - training_completion_percent; if training is UNKNOWN, set training_gap = 100.\n24\t  - cost_factor = min(10, total_direct_cost_usd / 10000).\n25\t\n26\tInputs for this CSV must be derived by:\n27\t- Parsing input/facilities.csv for facility roster and employees.\n28\t- Aggregating input/incidents.csv per facility: total_incidents, total_direct_cost_usd, avg_cost_per_incident_usd, total_lost_time_days.\n29\t- Summing asset values per facility from input/assets.jsonl.\n30\t- Inspecting the input/audits/ directory to find per-facility audit JSON files; if a facility’s audit file is missing, mark audit_compliance_percent as MISSING; otherwise parse compliance_percent from the file.\n31\t- Extracting facility_id and training_completion_percent from the HTML table in input/training.html; if a facility isn’t present in the table, set training_completion_percent to UNKNOWN.\n32\t\n33\t2) Create output/audit_inventory.txt that reflects directory inspection of input/audits/ using this structure:\n34\t- A section titled "Present audit files:" listing each found JSON file name on its own line.\n35\t- A section titled "Facilities missing audit files:" listing each facility_id with no corresponding audit JSON file on its own line.\n36\t\n37\t3) Create output/risk_summary.md that a chief can skim quickly. Include:\n38\t- A brief overview (1–3 sentences) stating inputs used and that this is for an insurance coverage decision.\n39\t- Company-wide totals: total incidents and total direct cost across all facilities (numbers only; direct cost rounded to 2 decimals).\n40\t- A "Top 3 facilities by composite risk score" section with a bullet list, each item including facility_id, facility_name, composite_risk_score, total_incidents, total_direct_cost_usd, audit_compliance_percent (or MISSING), and training_completion_percent (or UNKNOWN).\n41\t- A "Gaps/Notes" section that explicitly lists facilities without audit files and any facilities lacking training records.\n42\t\n43\tUse only the provided input files; do not fetch anything from the Internet. All outputs should be written to the output/ directory using the exact paths above. All file paths are relative to the workspace directory.\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14982240 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "Read", "arguments": {"file_path": "input/facilities.csv"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n1\tfacility_id,name,location,employees\n2\tF001,East Warehouse,Ohio,120\n3\tF002,West Plant,California,200\n4\tF003,Central Office,Illinois,80\n5\tF004,South Depot,Texas,60\n6\t\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14981298 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "Read", "arguments": {"file_path": "input/incidents.csv"}}\n</tool_call><|