(RolloutManager pid=4705) [2026-11-27 07:46:38] sglang_rollout.py:446 - Finish rollout: ['Read all files under input/ and complete four deliverables using only those snapshots (no external calls):\n\nFiles to use:\n- input/markets.json — market data snapshot (events with markets, prices, changes, volumes)\n- input/watchlist_spec.json — items to watch with thresholds and baselines\n- input/portfolio_seed.json — starting paper-portfolio state\n- input/trades.csv — buy/sell instructions\n\nTasks:\n1) Watchlist + Alerts\n- For each item in input/watchlist_spec.json, find the current Yes price from input/markets.json.\n- Compare current price to:\n  • alert_at_pct (e.g., 60 means trigger if current Yes price >= 0.60)\n  • alert_change_pct relative to baseline_price (trigger if abs((current-baseline)/baseline) >= alert_change_pct/100).\n- Outcome matching is case-insensitive and should match the market whose groupItemTitle equals the specified outcome when present; otherwise use the first market in the event.\n- Write output/watchlist.json with, for each item: { slug, outcome | null, baseline_price, current_price, alert_at_pct | null, alert_change_pct | null, triggered (bool), reasons (array of strings, using labels "alert_at" and/or "alert_change") }.\n- Also write output/alerts.json listing only the triggered items with a compact schema: [{ slug, outcome | null, current_price, reasons }].\n\n2) Category Digest (politics)\n- From input/markets.json, select events tagged as politics.\n- Sort these events by volume24hr descending and take the top 3.\n- For each event, select the single market with the highest current Yes price.\n- Write output/digest_politics.json as an array of 3 objects with fields: { slug, event_title, top_market_title, yes_price, oneDayPriceChange, volume24hr }.\n\n3) 24h Movers Report\n- Across all markets in input/markets.json, filter to events with volume24hr >= 10000.\n- Compute absolute oneDayPriceChange for each market and sort descending.\n- Output the top 5 to output/movers_24h.csv with header:\n  event_slug,event_title,market_title,yes_price,oneDayPriceChange,volume24hr\n- Rows must be ordered by absolute oneDayPriceChange descending.\n\n4) Paper Trading Simulation\n- Start from input/portfolio_seed.json (cash + positions array). Apply input/trades.csv in order, using current Yes prices from input/markets.json.\n- Trades format (CSV columns): action,slug,outcome,amount_type,amount_value. Rules:\n  • For buys with amount_type=usd: shares = amount_value / current_yes_price; subtract amount_value from cash; add/update position keyed by slug+outcome (outcome may be blank for single-market events).\n  • For sells with amount_type=fraction: sell that fraction of existing shares for that slug+outcome at current_yes_price; add proceeds to cash; reduce shares accordingly.\n- After applying all trades, compute total_value = cash + sum(shares * current_yes_price) across positions.\n- Write output/portfolio_after.json with: { cash, positions: [ { slug, outcome | null, shares, price } ], total_value }.\n- Also write output/portfolio_positions.csv with columns: slug,outcome,shares,current_price,market_value.\n\nFormatting:\n- All numeric values should be floats with at most 6 decimal places.\n- Use case-insensitive matching for outcomes.\n- Do not fetch anything from the internet; derive everything from the provided files.<tool_call>\n{"name": "Read", "arguments": {"file_path": "PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n1\tRead all files under input/ and complete four deliverables using only those snapshots (no external calls):\n2\t\n3\tFiles to use:\n4\t- input/markets.json — market data snapshot (events with markets, prices, changes, volumes)\n5\t- input/watchlist_spec.json — items to watch with thresholds and baselines\n6\t- input/portfolio_seed.json — starting paper-portfolio state\n7\t- input/trades.csv — buy/sell instructions\n8\t\n9\tTasks:\n10\t1) Watchlist + Alerts\n1