s_holiday_FR (true/false), is_holiday_MX (true/false), all_within_working_hours (true/false).\n  Use ISO 8601 timestamps with a Z suffix for UTC columns and explicit numeric offsets for local time columns.\n- outputs/summary.json: a summary that includes:\n  • considered_dates (array of YYYY‑MM‑DD),\n  • excluded_dates with reasons per date (e.g., weekend, FR holiday, MX holiday, no overlapping window),\n  • tz_offsets_used mapping each date to the UTC offsets you applied for Europe/Paris and America/Mexico_City,\n  • sources listing the exact file paths of the downloaded holiday JSON files and the compiled per‑zone offset JSON files, and\n  • selected_slots echoing the three proposals (slot_id and the same timestamps as in the CSV).\n\nValidation/cross‑checks:\n- selected_slots in outputs/summary.json must correspond exactly to the three rows in outputs/proposals.csv by slot_id and timestamps.\n- Do not propose any slot on a date that appears as a holiday in either web/holidays_FR_2025.json or web/holidays_MX_2025.json.\n- Do not propose any slot that would place any attendee outside their local working_start/working_end from the CSV.\n\nInput path:\n- input/attendees.csv (provided).\n\nPlease keep all new files under web/ and outputs/ as specified, and ensure the workflow is reproducible from the saved inputs and downloaded JSON. All file paths are relative to the workspace directory.<tool_call>\n{"name": "Read", "arguments": {"file_path": "PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n1\tI’m coordinating a cross‑time‑zone production check‑in with my Paris co‑producer and need a short list of concrete options that everyone can make. Please do the following using the attendees listed in input/attendees.csv.\n2\t\n3\tGoal and constraints:\n4\t- Propose exactly three 60‑minute meeting slots during Monday–Friday of 2025‑05‑12 through 2025‑05‑16 that all attendees can make. Each slot must:\n5\t  • fall entirely within every attende