list of extracted decisions (order preserved from transcript).\n     • Trivia Nuggets: bullet list of extracted trivia lines (order preserved).\n     • Action Items: bullet list of action items as "[owner] description (due: YYYY-MM-DD)"; unassigned items should show owner as "Unassigned".\n   - out/meetings/<target_date>/action_items.json: an array of objects with fields { id, description, owner, due_date, source, status, assignee_suggested? } where:\n     • id is a stable ID like A1, A2… in transcript order.\n     • owner is the validated participant name or "Unassigned" if not in participants.yaml.\n     • source = "transcript" for all items in this task.\n     • status = "open" for all items initially.\n     • assignee_suggested is included only when owner is "Unassigned".\n   - out/meetings/<target_date>/agenda_summary.csv: CSV with columns agenda_id,topic,presenter,type,meeting_date for the agenda rows matching the target_date.\n\n4) General:\n   - Make the script idempotent for the same target_date: repeated runs should produce the same outputs.\n   - Use only the provided local files; do not fetch anything from the Internet.\n\nRun against the included inputs as configured and write the outputs under out/meetings/2026-04-17/ so I can inspect the results. All file paths are relative to the workspace directory.<tool_call>\n{"name": "Read", "arguments": {"file_path": "PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n1\tI run a weekly "Assemblies & Politics Trivia" meetup and want to automate prep in a way that I can drop into cron later. Please build a small, cron‑friendly script that reads the provided local inputs and produces meeting notes and structured action items for the target date in input/run_config.json.\n2\t\n3\tRequirements:\n4\t1) Inputs (all relative to the workspace):\n5\t   - input/run_config.json: configuration with the target meeting date and input/output paths.\n6\t   - input/agenda.csv: agenda items for mul