(RolloutManager pid=4705) [2026-11-27 08:14:06] sglang_rollout.py:420 - First rollout sample: ["I'm a science fiction blogger trying to refine my content strategy using past performance and a new draft. Please do two things using the provided local files and save the results under the outputs directory.\n\nInputs:\n- input/posts.csv — historical post performance with columns: id,title,published_at,tags,words,views,likes,comments,shares\n- input/draft.html — an HTML draft of an upcoming post\n\nPart A — Tag performance summary (write to outputs/tag_summary.csv):\n- Read input/posts.csv and compute an engagement_rate for each post as (likes + comments + shares) / views.\n- Treat the tags field as a semicolon-separated list; include a post in each tag’s aggregation when it has multiple tags.\n- For each tag that appears in at least 2 posts, compute:\n  • post_count (number of posts tagged with it)\n  • median_views\n  • median_engagement_rate\n  • median_words\n  • pct_posts_above_overall_median_engagement = percentage of the tag’s posts whose engagement_rate is greater than or equal to the overall median engagement_rate across all posts\n- Output a CSV with a header row and the columns in this exact order: tag,post_count,median_views,median_engagement_rate,median_words,pct_posts_above_overall_median_engagement\n- Sort rows by median_engagement_rate (descending), breaking ties by median_views (descending).\n\nPart B — Draft structure extraction (write to outputs/draft_analysis.json):\n- Parse input/draft.html and analyze only visible text within the <article> element.\n- Extract:\n  • total_words: count of words in visible text (exclude tags, scripts, and attributes)\n  • estimated_reading_time_minutes: ceil(total_words / 220)\n  • heading_count_by_level: counts for h1, h2, and h3 in the article\n  • headings_extract: array of objects for each h1–h3 in document order with fields {level, text}\n  • max_heading_depth: the deepest heading level present among h1–h6 in the article (integer 1–6)\n  • images_count: number of <img> elements in the article\n  • total_links: number of <a> elements in the article\n  • outbound_links_by_domain: a mapping of domain to count for all <a> hrefs that are absolute http/https URLs (ignore relative links)\n- Save outputs/draft_analysis.json as a single JSON object with the above keys.\n\nNotes:\n- Assume views > 0 for all posts.\n- Use standard median (if even count, average the two middle values).\n- All outputs must be written to the outputs directory exactly as specified. All file paths are relative to the workspace directory."], label: clawgym_153, reward: 0.0
