(RolloutManager pid=4705) [2026-11-27 08:16:25] sglang_rollout.py:446 - Finish rollout: ['I need help syncing a cross-language next-sprint task summary for our team. Please work entirely in this workspace and use only the provided local files. Inputs to use:\n- input/backlog.csv (canonical backlog records)\n- input/team.json (assignee roles)\n- src/js/app.js and src/java/App.java (inline TODOs)\n- docs/README.md (update the marked section in place)\n\nRequirements:\n1) Inspect the directories src/js and src/java to extract TODOs that match exactly this pattern in comments:\n   // TODO[id=ID,priority=N,due=YYYY-MM-DD,assignee=NAME]: message\n   - Treat priority as an integer where 1 is highest.\n   - Derive language from file extension (.js -> "js", .java -> "java").\n   - Ignore any comments that don’t match the pattern above.\n\n2) Load and parse input/backlog.csv with columns:\n   id,title,component,language,priority,due,assignee,status\n   - Status values such as "open" and "done" are possible.\n\n3) Load input/team.json and enrich each task with assignee_role using the assignee’s role from team.json. If an assignee is not in team.json, set assignee_role to "Unknown".\n\n4) Merge and normalize tasks by id (case-sensitive):\n   - If a task id appears in both backlog and code, create a single unified record where title/component/language/priority/due/assignee/status come from the backlog, and include all code file paths where it was found.\n   - If a task id appears only in code, create a record with status="open", component="" (empty), language derived from the file extension, title set to the TODO message, and include the code file path.\n   - If a task id appears only in backlog, create a record using backlog fields and no code paths.\n   - Always attach assignee_role from team.json if available.\n\n5) Produce outputs/all_tasks.json containing an array of normalized task objects, sorted by id ascending, with these fields for each task:\n   - id (string)\n   - title (string)\n   - language (string)\n   - component (string; may be empty)\n   - priority (number)\n   - due (YYYY-MM-DD string)\n   - assignee (string)\n   - assignee_role (string)\n   - status ("open" or other)\n   - source (one of: "backlog", "code", "both")\n   - code_paths (array of file paths where found in code; empty array if none)\n\n6) Generate outputs/next_sprint.md with a table of the top 5 open tasks ranked strictly by:\n   - priority ascending (1 is highest), then\n   - due date ascending (earlier first), then\n   - id ascending (lexicographic)\n   Columns in this table must be: id, title, language, assignee, priority, due, source (use "both" if present in both backlog and code, otherwise "backlog" or "code"). Do not include tasks with status != "open" in this ranking.\n\n7) Edit docs/README.md in-place: replace everything between the markers\n   <!-- NEXT_SPRINT_START -->\n   and\n   <!-- NEXT_SPRINT_END -->\n   with exactly the same table content generated in outputs/next_sprint.md (same columns and rows). Do not modify any other part of README.\n\nNotes and constraints:\n- Only consider files within src/js and src/java for TODO extraction.\n- Do not add arbitrary tasks; only use what is in input/backlog.csv and the matching TODOs found in the code files.\n- Ensure all outputs are deterministic given the provided inputs.\n- Make sure both outputs/all_tasks.json and outputs/next_sprint.md are created, and docs/README.md is updated as specified. All file paths are relative to the workspace directory.'], label: clawgym_060, reward: 0.0
